cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent instruction files: measuring whether declared rules change code compliance"
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Takatbek
    given-names: Yerkhat
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yerkhat1/agent-instruction-files"
abstract: >-
  Compliance measured across 753 rules declared in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md files
  in 410 public Python repositories, using static analysis at the commit where
  each rule first appears and at HEAD. Two thirds of rules were declared against
  code that already complied. Among rules declared below ceiling, those backed by
  enforcement tooling closed roughly three times more of the remaining gap than
  rules stated only in prose, with no difference in how much of the codebase was
  edited.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - ai agents
  - empirical software engineering
  - mining software repositories
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-06"
